# Licensing

Zeo is a fork of [KiCad](https://kicad.org) and bundles several upstream
projects. The project **as a whole is offered under the GNU Affero General
Public License, version 3** (AGPLv3) — see [`LICENSE`](LICENSE).

## What the AGPLv3 covers

The AGPLv3 applies to **Zeo's own creations and modifications**: original code,
features, and changes authored by the Zeo project. These files carry a Zeo
copyright notice and are licensed under AGPLv3.

## Upstream and third-party code

Zeo does **not** relicense upstream code. Every incorporated component —
KiCad, freerouting, wxWidgets, the packaging projects, and the third-party
libraries vendored within them — **retains its original license**. The
authoritative terms for any given file are stated in that file's own header
and in the license files shipped within each component (for example, the
`LICENSE.*` files under `src/zeo`). Nothing in this document overrides those
notices.

## How the licenses combine

AGPLv3 and GPLv3 are explicitly cross-compatible: section 13 of each license
permits combining works under the other into a single combined work. The
upstream GPL-licensed code stays under its own terms, Zeo's own code is
AGPLv3, and the combined work, as conveyed by Zeo, is governed by the
AGPLv3.

## Trademark

"KiCad" is a trademark of its owners. Zeo is an independent fork and is not
affiliated with or endorsed by the KiCad project.
